/E (During ballet pointe work, dancers must maintain foot and ankle alignments while supporting their body weight on a very small contact area. Small deviations from the optimal alignment like sickling \(inversion and adduction of the rearfoot with lateral malleolus misalignment\) or rolling \(excessive load on the first or fifth metatarsal\) alter how forces transmit through the foot-ankle complex, increasing the risk of ankle sprains, tendonitis, stress fractures and reduced postural stability.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [98]
>>
